# LaTeX build artifacts
**/*.aux
**/*.log
**/*.out
**/*.bbl
**/*.blg
**/*.toc
**/*.fdb_latexmk
**/*.fls
**/*.synctex.gz
**/missfont.log

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# scratch / temp
_new_*.jsonl
_refactor_*.jsonl
_fix_*.jsonl

# Run outputs: 16M of records+transcripts per session. Kept on disk (they are the generation cache
# and the evidence base) but out of git, matching how this repo already treats benchmark/result,
# caesar/*result and test/result. result/readme.md stays tracked.
result/runs/
result/index.jsonl
result/latest
result/.stall_state.json
# Aborted runs are archived out of runs/ so the cache and the health checks stop seeing them, but
# their records are the same 100s-of-KB payload and must stay out of git for the same reason.
# The readme is NOT ignored: it is the only record of why each was aborted and what its records
# cannot be used for, which is worth versioning even though the data behind it is not.
result/aborted/*/
!result/aborted/readme.md

# Dataset working copies. git is the diff trail once committed; every audit correction is also
# recorded old->new in doc/misc/hallucination_audit_live_log.jsonl.
question/*.bak_*
question/crest_challenges.pre_audit.jsonl
question/crest_challenges.audit.jsonl

# LaTeX output PDFs are build artifacts (regenerate with paper/compile.sh)
**/main.pdf
